                <pb facs="1299" n="1293" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1293"/>

                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">January</hi> 22, 1894.—Referred
                    to the Committee on Foreign Affairs and ordered to be printed.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">The Congress:</hi>]</p>
                <p>I transmit herewith copies of dispatches received from our minister to Hawaii
                    after the arrival of those, copies of which accompanied my message of the 20th
                    instant.</p>
                <p>I also inclose for the information of the Congress copies of reports and a copy
                    of an order just received by the Secretary of the Navy from Rear-Admiral Irwin,
                    commanding our naval forces at Honolulu.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grover Cleveland.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Executive
                            Mansion</hi>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-01-22"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">January 22, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
